# A value that is stored into a slot of a scope either has been shown to have the slot's type or is checked. Link types the slot of `n` by the stores that it sees,
# the plan gives the slot a raw representation based on that type, and every function that closes over the scope reads the slot without a check.
# The failing control. Fault injection, testing=AssumeUnknownCallsReturnUndefined: Link assumes that the shell's `id` returns undefined, so `n` holds a number or undefined, but a string is stored.
# In the first run the setter's body stores the string. It used to print "NaN" and continue.
# In the second and the third run the setter is called with an argument of another type than the declared one, so its slow version runs.
# Straight code converts a value to the slot's representation without a check, so such a version goes through the walk, and the entry check is there too.
# OPTIONS: testing=AssumeUnknownCallsReturnUndefined
# RUN(WALKED): run-in-shell mechanisms=all-Inlining globalThis.which = 1;
# WALKED: bun: internal AOT error: type check failed
# WALKED-NEXT: found string in a closure variable
# WALKED-NOT: went on
# WALKED: crashed with
# RUN(SLOW): run-in-shell mechanisms=all-Inlining globalThis.which = 2;
# SLOW: bun: internal AOT error: type check failed
# SLOW-NEXT: found string in a closure variable
# SLOW-NOT: went on
# SLOW: crashed with
# RUN(CELL): run-in-shell mechanisms=all-Inlining globalThis.which = 3;
# CELL: bun: internal AOT error: type check failed
# CELL-NEXT: found int32 in a closure variable
# CELL-NOT: went on
# CELL: crashed with
# The passing control: the same stores, of values that fit.
# RUN(NONE): run-in-shell mechanisms=all globalThis.which = 0;
# NONE: 2.5 leaf
# NONE-NEXT: went on
# NONE-NEXT: exited with 0
# -- source: a-false-proof-of-a-slot-of-a-scope-is-stopped-in-every-build.ts
